**user**:
> I have started a plan to build an abstraction around model and tool selection in my AI system. Here is the contract for tools:
> """
> Tool protocol and normalized typed tool-result contract.
> 
> Tools are executable capabilities. In the initial synchronous system they may
> be invoked directly by a responder. In the workflow system they are executed
> as Operations and yield Artifacts. Tool interfaces should therefore avoid
> assuming that their primary result is user-visible text.
> 
> Expected tool callable shape:
> 
> ToolCallable = Callable[
>     [ToolInvocation],
>     ToolResult,
> ]
> 
> @dataclass(frozen=True)
> class ToolInvocation:
>     operation_id: str | None
>     conversation_id: str
>     arguments: Mapping[str, Any]
>     config: Mapping[str, Any]
>     context: PlannerContext | None
>     provenance_requirements: Mapping[str, Any]
> 
> @dataclass
> class Tool:
>     name: str
>     description: str
>     fn: ToolCallable | Callable[..., Any]
>     config: ToolConfig
>     quality_prior: float | None = None
>     cost_estimate: float | None = None
>     version: str = "1"
> 
> Compatibility:
> - registry.py may accept legacy functions such as
>   `fn(prompt, config) -> str`.
> - tools/base.py normalizes such outputs to ToolResult/Artifact.
> - Tool configuration defaults and allowed discrete options are validated here.
> 
> Caller:
> - responders.py or workflow/workers.py invokes:
>       result = tool.fn(invocation)
> - the caller persists raw temporary output as appropriate, converts relevant
>   materials to artifacts/source excerpts, and never blindly injects untrusted
>   tool text into system instructions.
> """
> 
> Now, here is the documentation for a tool available through OpenAI:
> ## Computer use
> 
> `computer` returns structured mouse and keyboard actions for a browser or desktop that you run; you execute them and send back a screenshot. The tool takes no configuration fields in the current docs. For GPT-6 Astra, OpenAI now recommends a code-execution harness (a `function` tool that runs Playwright or PyAutoGUI scripts) instead.
> 
> ```python
> resp = client.responses.create(
>     model="gpt-5.6-sol",
>     tools=[{"type": "computer"}],
>     input="Open the Filters panel if needed, then search for penguin.",
> )
> # then, for each computer_call:
> client.responses.create(
>     model="gpt-5.6-sol",
>     tools=[{"type": "computer"}],
>     previous_response_id=resp.id,
>     input=[{"type": "computer_call_output", "call_id": call_id,
>             "output": {"type": "computer_screenshot",
>                        "image_url": f"data:image/png;base64,{png_b64}",
>                        "detail": "original"}}],
> )
> ```
> 
> Each `computer_call` holds an ordered `actions` array. Action types: `click` (with `button`, `x`, `y`), `double_click`, `drag`, `move`, `scroll`, `keypress`, `type` (with `text`), `wait`, `screenshot`. Run it in an isolated VM or browser and confirm consequential actions with a human.
> 
> Can you construct a full tool implementation for this? Please start off the file with a docstring, describing the tool and its usage.
**assistant**:
> ```python
> """
> OpenAI Computer tool adapter.
> 
> This tool asks an OpenAI Responses model to plan browser/desktop interactions
> using OpenAI's `computer` tool. It does *not* execute mouse or keyboard actions
> itself. Instead, it returns structured `computer_call` action batches as
> artifacts; a trusted, isolated browser/VM executor must execute them.
> 
> Usage:
>     tool = make_openai_computer_tool(client, model="gpt-5.6-sol")
> 
>     result = tool.fn(ToolInvocation(
>         operation_id="op_123",
>         conversation_id="conv_123",
>         arguments={"input": "Search for penguins."},
>         config={},
>         context=None,
>         provenance_requirements={},
>     ))
> 
> For continuation after executing actions, invoke it with
> `previous_response_id` and `computer_call_outputs`, where each output includes
> the original call ID and an executor-captured screenshot data URL. Never allow
> the model to directly control a non-isolated host, and require human approval
> for consequential actions.
> """
> 
> from __future__ import annotations
> 
> import base64
> from dataclasses import asdict, is_dataclass
> from typing import Any, Mapping, Sequence
> 
> from .base import Artifact, ToolResult
> from .registry import Tool, ToolConfig
> from .types import ToolInvocation
> 
> 
> _MAX_SCREENSHOT_BYTES = 20 * 1024 * 1024
> 
> 
> def make_openai_computer_tool(
>     client: Any,
>     *,
>     model: str = "gpt-5.6-sol",
>     name: str = "openai_computer",
> ) -> Tool:
>     """Create a normalized OpenAI computer-planning tool.
> 
>     `client` should be an initialized OpenAI client. Keep credentials and model
>     selection in application configuration rather than tool invocation inputs.
>     """
> 
>     def invoke(invocation: ToolInvocation) -> ToolResult:
>         args = dict(invocation.arguments)
>         prompt = args.get("input")
>         previous_response_id = args.get("previous_response_id")
>         outputs = args.get("computer_call_outputs")
> 
>         if prompt is None and not outputs:
>             return _failure("invalid_arguments", "Provide `input` or computer_call_outputs.")
>         if prompt is not None and not isinstance(prompt, (str, list)):
>             return _failure("invalid_arguments", "`input` must be a string or Responses input list.")
>         if previous_response_id is not None and not isinstance(previous_response_id, str):
>             return _failure("invalid_arguments", "`previous_response_id` must be a string.")
> 
>         try:
>             continuation_input = _build_continuation_outputs(outputs) if outputs else prompt
> 
>             request: dict[str, Any] = {
>                 "model": model,
>                 "tools": [{"type": "computer"}],
>                 "input": continuation_input,
>             }
>             if previous_response_id:
>                 request["previous_response_id"] = previous_response_id
> 
>             response = client.responses.create(**request)
>         except ValueError as exc:
>             return _failure("invalid_arguments", str(exc))
>         except Exception as exc:
>             # Do not expose credentials, headers, or arbitrary provider payloads.
>             return _failure("openai_request_failed", f"{type(exc).__name__}: {exc}")
> 
>         response_id = getattr(response, "id", None)
>         calls = _extract_computer_calls(response)
> 
>         artifacts = [
>             Artifact(
>                 kind="computer_action_batch",
>                 mime_type="application/json",
>                 data={
>                     "response_id": response_id,
>                     "call_id": call["call_id"],
>                     "actions": call["actions"],
>                     "status": call["status"],
>                 },
>                 metadata={
>                     "provider": "openai",
>                     "tool": "computer",
>                     "model": model,
>                     "operation_id": invocation.operation_id,
>                     "conversation_id": invocation.conversation_id,
>                     "untrusted": True,
>                 },
>             )
>             for call in calls
>         ]
> 
>         return ToolResult(
>             success=True,
>             artifacts=artifacts,
>             data={
>                 "response_id": response_id,
>                 "computer_call_count": len(calls),
>                 # Text is deliberately not promoted to instructions.
>                 "output_text": getattr(response, "output_text", None),
>             },
>             error=None,
>         )
> 
>     return Tool(
>         name=name,
>         description=(
>             "Requests structured browser/desktop actions from OpenAI Computer. "
>             "Actions must be executed only by an isolated, trusted executor."
>         ),
>         fn=invoke,
>         config=ToolConfig(defaults={}, allowed_options={}),
>         quality_prior=0.8,
>         cost_estimate=None,
>         version="1",
>     )
> 
> 
> def _build_continuation_outputs(outputs: Any) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:
>     if not isinstance(outputs, Sequence) or isinstance(outputs, (str, bytes)):
>         raise ValueError("`computer_call_outputs` must be a list.")
> 
>     result: list[dict[str, Any]] = []
>     for item in outputs:
>         if not isinstance(item, Mapping):
>             raise ValueError("Each computer_call_output must be an object.")
> 
>         call_id = item.get("call_id")
>         image_url = item.get("image_url")
>         detail = item.get("detail", "original")
> 
>         if not isinstance(call_id, str) or not call_id:
>             raise ValueError("Each computer_call_output requires a non-empty `call_id`.")
>         if not isinstance(image_url, str) or not image_url.startswith("data:image/"):
>             raise ValueError("Screenshots must be image data URLs.")
>         if len(image_url) > (_MAX_SCREENSHOT_BYTES * 4 // 3):
>             raise ValueError("Screenshot exceeds maximum permitted size.")
> 
>         result.append(
>             {
>                 "type": "computer_call_output",
>                 "call_id": call_id,
>                 "output": {
>                     "type": "computer_screenshot",
>                     "image_url": image_url,
>                     "detail": detail,
>                 },
>             }
>         )
>     return result
> 
> 
> def _extract_computer_calls(response: Any) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:
>     calls: list[dict[str, Any]] = []
> 
>     for item in getattr(response, "output", []) or []:
>         item_type = getattr(item, "type", None)
>         if item_type != "computer_call":
>             continue
> 
>         raw_actions = getattr(item, "actions", []) or []
>         actions = [
>             _jsonable(action)
>             for action in raw_actions
>             if getattr(action, "type", None) in {
>                 "click", "double_click", "drag", "move", "scroll",
>                 "keypress", "type", "wait", "screenshot",
>             }
>         ]
> 
>         calls.append(
>             {
>                 "call_id": getattr(item, "call_id", None) or getattr(item, "id", None),
>                 "status": getattr(item, "status", None),
>                 "actions": actions,
>             }
>         )
> 
>     return calls
> 
> 
> def _jsonable(value: Any) -> Any:
>     if hasattr(value, "model_dump"):
>         return value.model_dump(mode="json")
>     if is_dataclass(value):
>         return asdict(value)
>     if isinstance(value, Mapping):
>         return {str(k): _jsonable(v) for k, v in value.items()}
>     if isinstance(value, (list, tuple)):
>         return [_jsonable(v) for v in value]
>     return value
> 
> 
> def _failure(code: str, message: str) -> ToolResult:
>     return ToolResult(
>         success=False,
>         artifacts=[],
>         data={},
>         error={"code": code, "message": message},
>     )
> ```
> 
> The executor should treat `computer_action_batch` artifacts as untrusted requests, enforce allowlists and approval gates, execute only in an isolated environment, and supply the resulting screenshot through `computer_call_outputs`.
